-- An imported record alias's implicit constructor builds the RECORD,
-- as in Elm (language.md §0; checker-v2.md §14.2, the record-alias
-- constructor rows; the owner's decision for its representation). `P 1 "a"` is a
-- `{ x : Int, y : String }`, so `.y` reads `"a"`. Expected `a`.
--
-- Oracle twin: this project with `p = { x = 1, y = "a" }`
-- in place of the constructor call prints `a`. Typing every imported
-- constructor as a nominal would refuse it with TYPE MISMATCH "This is not
-- a record with a `y` field: It is: `P`".
import Node exposing (Program)
import Pt exposing (P)


p = P 1 "a"


main : Program
main = Node.printLines [ p.y ]
